    "Social: client API" : "Social: client API",
    "Mastodon apps can reach this instance." : "Mastodon apps can reach this instance.",
    "Nothing usable answers at /api/v1/instance, so Mastodon apps cannot add an account here: they build their addresses from the domain alone and never use the /index.php/apps/social prefix these routes live under. The web server has to map /api, /oauth and /.well-known/host-meta onto the app. %1$s Everything else — the web interface and federation with other servers — works without this." : "Nothing usable answers at /api/v1/instance, so Mastodon apps cannot add an account here: they build their addresses from the domain alone and never use the /index.php/apps/social prefix these routes live under. The web server has to map /api, /oauth and /.well-known/host-meta onto the app. %1$s Everything else — the web interface and federation with other servers — works without this.",
    "%1$s/api/v1/instance answered %2$d. If the rules are in place, check that what they proxy to serves this Nextcloud: a rule pointing at a port or a host that serves a different document root answers 404 exactly as a missing rule does. An Apache 404 page names the port it came from, which tells the two apart." : "%1$s/api/v1/instance answered %2$d. If the rules are in place, check that what they proxy to serves this Nextcloud: a rule pointing at a port or a host that serves a different document root answers 404 exactly as a missing rule does. An Apache 404 page names the port it came from, which tells the two apart.",
